       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. A dose of 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. That is far above the 4 g/day maximum and could cause acute liver failure in a patient with normal liver function. I can't enter an order I expect to seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** Give me the dose you want, such as 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 1000 mg every 6 hours (4 g/day).\n- **Add a note.** I can put a clinical rationale in the order note if you have a specific reason for the dose.\n- **Escalate.** If you think this dose is intended, for example for a protocol I don't know about, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or the attending first. Their review would go through the usual safety checks.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
